---
import StaticPageLayout from "../../layouts/StaticPageLayout.astro";
import { contactEmail, globalPaths, siteUrl } from "../../data/site-shell";

const schema = [
	{
		"@context": "https://schema.org",
		"@type": "AboutPage",
		name: "About treespuzzle.com",
		url: `${siteUrl}${globalPaths.about}`,
		description:
			"Background, editorial purpose, and update approach for the independent HER TREES information site.",
	},
	{
		"@context": "https://schema.org",
		"@type": "BreadcrumbList",
		itemListElement: [
			{
				"@type": "ListItem",
				position: 1,
				name: "Home",
				item: siteUrl,
			},
			{
				"@type": "ListItem",
				position: 2,
				name: "About",
				item: `${siteUrl}${globalPaths.about}`,
			},
		],
	},
];
---

<StaticPageLayout
	title="About Her Trees Puzzle Dream - Independent Play Hub"
	description="Independent site for Her Trees Puzzle Dream: play free in the browser, keypad walkthroughs, Puzzle House, and First Puzzle. Not the official developer site."
	canonicalPath={globalPaths.about}
	pageHeading="About This Site"
	pageIntro="treespuzzle.com is an independent editorial project built to help players understand the HER TREES puzzle series before they decide where and how to play it."
	breadcrumbLabel="About"
	schema={schema}
>
	<p>
		This website was created as a focused reference hub for a small puzzle-game
		series that can otherwise be difficult to evaluate at a glance. The HER TREES
		games rely on mood, hand-drawn art, and non-verbal puzzle language, so many
		players want a compact explanation of the tone, expected playtime, and
		accessibility before they commit to a download or purchase. The goal here is
		to provide that context in one place.
	</p>
	<p>
		The site is not an official publisher or developer property. It is an
		independent editorial website that curates publicly visible information,
		writes original summaries, and organizes gameplay notes for visitors who want a
		clear overview. When this site links to Steam, itch.io, YouTube, or the
		browser build of a game, those links are provided for convenience and do not
		change the ownership of the underlying intellectual property.
	</p>
	<h3>What readers should expect</h3>
	<p>
		Content on treespuzzle.com is written to answer practical player questions:
		what the game feels like, what kind of puzzle logic it uses, whether it is
		text-heavy, how long it lasts, and where to play. Start with
		<a href="/play/puzzle-dream/">Her Trees Puzzle Dream</a> in the browser, use the
		<a href="/play/puzzle-dream/guide/">Dream keypad walkthrough</a> if you are stuck,
		or open <a href="/play/puzzle-house/">Puzzle House</a> and
		<a href="/play/first-puzzle/">First Puzzle</a>.
	</p>
	<p>
		We aim to keep the writing concise but useful. Instead of publishing thin
		announcement posts, the site focuses on evergreen pages that help visitors make
		a decision. That means we prefer updated comparison tables, explanation of the
		series structure, and carefully framed spoiler notices over filler content that
		does not help the reader.
	</p>
	<h3>How the site is maintained</h3>
	<p>
		Pages are updated when the public-facing status of the series changes, such as
		a release date update, a newly available demo, or a meaningful change to where
		a title can be played. We also revise pages when a section becomes unclear,
		under-documented, or too dependent on outside embeds. Editorial changes are
		made to improve clarity and usefulness first.
	</p>
	<p>
		If you are the rights holder and believe a factual correction, attribution
		change, or asset removal is needed, please contact
		<a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>. Requests tied to
		trademarks, screenshots, or copyright claims are reviewed as a priority.
	</p>
	<h3>What is original on this site</h3>
	<p>
		The structure, summaries, feature explanations, guide framing, spoiler notes,
		and editorial commentary on treespuzzle.com are original writing prepared for
		this site. Game titles, trademarks, screenshots, platform names, and public
		release facts belong to their respective owners. We separate site commentary
		from the underlying game property on purpose so visitors can understand what is
		editorial interpretation and what is source material.
	</p>
</StaticPageLayout>
